# docs/agents

Agent rules. The root `AGENTS.md` is short and works as navigation; the details live here. The agent reads a document when the work falls into its area (the "Navigation" table in `AGENTS.md`).

| Document | When to read |
| --- | --- |
| [repository-layout.md](repository-layout.md) | Before working with clones and when choosing where to start the agent |
| [tooling.md](tooling.md) | Before changing `mise.toml`, `repos.toml`, tasks, hooks, sdd-kit, `ast-grep` rules and root tests |
| [agent-settings.md](agent-settings.md) | Before changing `.claude/`, permissions, agent hooks |
| [branches.md](branches.md) | Before creating a branch, a commit or a pull request |
| [ticket-workflow.md](ticket-workflow.md) | {% if tracker != 'none' %}Working a {{ tracker_name }} ticket: reading it, questions, when and how to open a pull request{% else %}When and how to open a pull request{% endif %} |
| [environment.md](environment.md) | Before running the applications and their tests |

## Writing documents in this folder

A document answers one question and starts with it. Rules are written as statements, each with a reason. Anything a command checks names that command. Do not duplicate `AGENTS.md`; a link is enough.
